(46450, '11', '2', '6', 'o1', '1) all stores will have the same hours of operation. This can be a single setting for all locations. 10am - 6pm CST is our standard time frame.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n2) yes, I’d expect each location to have an inventory field that can be manually adjusted when using “local pickup” vs “Ship to Store” delivery options.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n3) Yes, all functions are working based on my tests. If you’d like to see this live, use the zip code 54024.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso, I am finalizing my decision soon with the developer team we will work with.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI’ve detailed the scope of work. Does this look accurate to you?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n=== Scope of Work ===\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n“Ship to Store” Functionality:\r\n• Create a shipping method named \"Ship to Store.\"\r\n• Display predefined store locations in a list using WooCommerce’s default radio buttons (store name and address).\r\n• Lock the shipping address to the selected store location and disable the shipping address fields at checkout.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLocal vs. Warehouse Inventory Management:\r\n• Prioritize local store inventory for immediate pickup.\r\n• If local inventory is unavailable, fallback to warehouse inventory and ship to the selected store.\r\n• Ensure compatibility with the SparkShipping API for warehouse inventory updates.\r\n• Display accurate stock availability based on local or warehouse inventory dynamically.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSeamless Checkout Workflow:\r\n• Pre-select the first store location if \"Local Pickup\" is the only shipping option.\r\n• Allow switching of store locations from the cart page only.\r\n• Standard WooCommerce checkout experience with no disruption to other functionalities.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStore Management:\r\n• Flexibility to add or update predefined store locations through plugin settings.\r\n• Support dynamic updates for store locations and inventory management.', NULL, '2024-12-11 10:32:30', '2024-12-11 11:17:07', '2024-12-11', '00:44:37', NULL, NULL),
