(46855, '2', '2', '5', 'o1', 'With Deep', NULL, '2024-12-16 07:12:55', '2024-12-16 07:32:03', '2024-12-16', '00:19:08', NULL, NULL),
(46856, '7', '2', '2', 'o1', 'Thank you very much Parth! You and your team sound like a great fit for this project. Your hours and cost estimations are fair as well as reasonable.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease keep in mind in your SOW, you do not need to do anything with the Spark Shipping API for inventory updates as this function is already working great. This should reduce or simplify your SOW and hours needed. I’d rather make sure this plugin is simple, clean, and easy to maintain with the least amount of customization as possible.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI’d like to keep this as simple as possible while still getting the data we need, especially given our tight budget.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIdeally, we can add two filters to the existing WooCommerce reporting pages:\r\n1. Location (primary filter - mapped to static ip address of location)\r\n2. Employee (secondary filter - comes from product order field - who are you working with or similar question)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis would allow us to easily see revenue numbers by location and drill down by employee within that location. If integrating these filters into the native WooCommerce reports isn’t feasible, a simple custom reporting page within the location plugin would work, as long as it provides similar functionality. The simpler the solution, the better, and I prefer to rely on WooCommerce’s native features wherever possible.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAdditionally, it would be helpful to include a custom field on the product or ordering page where team members can enter their name (e.g., “Who referred you?”). This would allow us to track revenue by location and then within that location by employee.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIn summary, my goal is straightforward:\r\n• Revenue by Location\r\n• Revenue by Employee (within Location)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor shipping options, I want to confirm we have the following clearly defined:\r\n1. Delivery: Default WooCommerce option, ships directly to the customer from the warehouse.\r\n2. Local Pickup: Default WooCommerce option, inventory available for pickup at a store location.\r\n3. Ship to Store: New feature that ships inventory from the warehouse to a store for later pickup.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLastly, I like the idea of adding a “Pickup Today” label for products with local pickup inventory available at a store. This would make it clear to customers which items are ready for immediate pickup.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor reporting, a simple grid view would suffice for now, as charts and visuals can be added later if the budget allows.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLet me know your thoughts. Thank you for your time.', NULL, '2024-12-16 07:13:07', '2024-12-16 07:32:58', '2024-12-16', '00:19:50', NULL, NULL),
