(46963, '7', '2', '3', 'o1', 'Thank you very much! It’s great to have a clear SOW for both of us. Answers below\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n1) - Question answer: pickup today label seen on product grid page, search results pages, and any product pages. No need to have on order details page or cart page.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n2) - Employee filter: employee list can be a dropdown of employee names to choose as an optional field. We should be able to edit this on the backend if needed.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n3) - IP addresses: We don’t need the script for country. We block all non-USA traffic via cloudflare.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n4) - Filters: We really would like the filters on the native reports areas for location and employee filter. Having a separate grid is ok but not as preferred for a custom report in the plugin for locations/staff. I’m flexible if needed but native is best. Location and employee filters would be best under date selection box in analytics. Defaults for both filters should include all locations and employees unless selected.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n5) - Inventory from local pickup and warehouse: If a client wants 5 items and only 3 are available for local pickup and 2 items are in the warehouse. Both inventory locations would be used. 3 local pickup items would be on a single order line. Then the other 2 coming from the warehouse would be a separate line order in the shopping cart page. This would need to be the logic to ensure native order tracking and notifications work within the default functions of Woocommerce. It needs to be smart enough to pull items from both places in the event a client wants to buy more than what is available from a location (fulfill additional quantities if available from warehouse inventory with ship to store functionality). It might be helpful to provide visibility of both? Following Walmart.coms process, they more show a single inventory until it’s gone. Then they offer alternative fulfillment like “ship to store” when “local pickup” is out of stock. Users could also select “ship to home” (whatever the default delivery/shipping is with Woocommerce) to ship direct to then if enabled in shipping zones. I’m open to your suggestion.', NULL, '2024-12-17 04:11:50', '2024-12-17 05:01:36', '2024-12-17', '00:49:45', NULL, NULL),
