(69944, '7', '2', '2', 'o1', 'for sanjana \r\n\r\nHi Deep,\r\n \r\nThanks for the architecture and the screenshots Sanjana shared. I’ve reviewed them—overall the Woo hook → Node.js worker → Playwright → Proton Bridge → Google Sheets flow and the 10-minute SLA approach make sense.\r\n \r\nBefore we proceed, please confirm/provide:\r\n \r\nSLA/SLO details\r\n– Exact success criteria for the 10-min SLA (p95/p99) and what counts as “delivered.”\r\n– Failure matrix with retry/backoff limits and admin-escalation path.\r\n \r\nSecurity\r\n– Where creds/TOTP secrets live, encryption at rest/in transit, access controls, audit logs.\r\n– Credential rotation runbook + rollback plan (you note “keep last 2 sets”—confirm how long).\r\n \r\nMonitoring & Alerts\r\n– Heartbeats for Proton Bridge + panel login: frequency, thresholds, alert channels (email/SMS/Slack webhook).\r\n– Sample alert payloads and who is paged.\r\n \r\nIdempotency & Data\r\n– Memo/idempotency token format and dedupe guarantees across crashes/restarts.\r\n– Data retention policy for logs and customer data.\r\n \r\nHandover & Ownership\r\n– Code ownership (repo access, license), deploy guides, runbooks, and acceptance test plan.\r\n– Warranty/support window post-go-live.\r\n \r\nDelivery Plan\r\n– Milestones, timeline, demo date for an end-to-end sandbox run (mock order → email sent).\r\n– Budget/quote with scope boundaries; assumptions & out-of-scope list.\r\n– Links to the promised code samples/Gists.\r\n \r\nIf you can package the above into a brief SoW with milestones and acceptance criteria, I can approve quickly.\r\n \r\nThanks,\r\nMO', NULL, '2025-09-17 08:26:25', '2025-09-17 09:07:04', '2025-09-17', '00:40:39', NULL, NULL),
