(70860, '2', '1', '4', NULL, 'The GCLID (Google Click ID) is generated whenever someone clicks on our Google Ads and lands on the website. It is passed in the landing page URL (e.g., ?gclid=xxxxxx).\r\nTo make it available in the backend:\r\nWhen the visitor first submits the quote form, the GCLID from the URL needs to be captured and saved in the PrestaShop database together with the quote/order record.\r\nLater, when the quote status changes to “Devis validé,” the stored GCLID can be sent via Zapier (or API) into Google Ads as the identifier for that conversion.\r\nIn short, the GCLID is not automatically in the backend — it must be captured at the time of form submission and then stored for later use.\r\nOnce your developer captures and stores the GCLID with each quote, I can ensure Zapier sends only the validated ones into Google Ads.', NULL, '2025-09-25 12:02:21', '2025-09-25 13:24:27', '2025-09-25', '01:22:06', NULL, NULL),
