(74691, '2', '2', '8', 'o1', 'Just to clarify, my application will be different from Getaround.\r\nIt will not be a peer-to-peer car-sharing platform where individual owners rent out their vehicles.\r\n \r\nIn my case, I now have my own company that provides its own vehicle(s) for rental — a model closer to Rentcar (https://www.rentacar.fr/?wiz_medium=sea&wiz_source=google&wiz_campaign=419132226&wiz_term=rent%20a%20car&msclkid=3190b81b925716d1af96d1180c6f7160&utm_source=bing&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=SN%20-%20Marque%20Exact&utm_term=rent%20a%20car&utm_content=Marque_E) or Sixt (https://www.sixt.fr/?sxamc=Bing|Search&fir=1&utm_campaignid=283505996&utm_adgroupid=1244647547365010&msclkid=66fcd8656de91b43c5fdb166f00c0fba&utm_source=bing&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=FR%20-%20FR_rent_BRAND%20Pure_(FRE)&utm_term=sixt%20location&utm_content=FR%20-%20FR%20BRAND%20Pure).\r\n \r\nFor now, there is only one vehicle available, and the idea is that users can:\r\n \r\nview the car photos,\r\n \r\nmake a reservation,\r\n \r\ncomplete everything directly within the app.\r\n \r\nOf course, we’ll take inspiration from Getaround in terms of design, user flow, and booking process.\r\n \r\nIf needed, I can share my Getaround account credentials so that you can explore the platform from the owner’s perspective for reference.\r\n \r\nBest regards,\r\nSamuel', NULL, '2025-11-03 07:06:54', '2025-11-03 08:02:29', '2025-11-03', '00:55:35', NULL, NULL),
